{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>YHWH will reign</b> — a break, to tell you: when the time comes that they say 'YHWH reigned, YHWH reigns, YHWH will reign forever and ever,' then the dominion of Esau-Rome will cease. Moses placed YHWH before kingship, and David placed kingship before YHWH, as stated: 'YHWH will reign forever.' Because he concluded with 'and the way of the wicked shall be crooked,' he did not wish to mention the name of YHWH upon evil."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:13:04.712755138Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}